<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Entropy Rates for Score-Based Diffusion Models</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Seifert’s original formulation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Seifert, 2012</a>]</cite> and subsequent applications to diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ikeda et al., 2025</a>]</cite> motivate the mathematical framework we adopt here.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Current-score-drift identity</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the general overdamped SDE <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{f}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)dt+g(t)d\mathbf{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{f}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)dt+g(t)d\mathbf{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability current is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})-D(t)\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=p_{t}(\mathbf{x})[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-D(t)\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})-D(t)\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=p_{t}(\mathbf{x})[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-D(t)\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we have used <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)^{2}=2D(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)^{2}=2D(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})=\nabla\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})=\nabla\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\nabla\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\nabla\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>. The local velocity field is defined as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x},t):=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-D(t)\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)=\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)/p_{t}(\mathbf{x})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x},t):=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-D(t)\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)=\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)/p_{t}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Intrinsic entropy-production rate</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Seifert [2012]</a></cite>’s original expression for the intrinsic entropy production rate is given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{S}^{i}(t)=\int\frac{\left\|\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|^{2}}{D(t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\frac{1}{D(t)}\int p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\left\|\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|^{2}d\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{S}^{i}(t)=\int\frac{\left\|\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|^{2}}{D(t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\frac{1}{D(t)}\int p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\left\|\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|^{2}d\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In expectation notation,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{S}^{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{S}^{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D(t)}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]=\frac{2}{g(t)^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D(t)}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]=\frac{2}{g(t)^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2g(t)^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\|2\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-g(t)^{2}\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2g(t)^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\|2\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-g(t)^{2}\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Exchange (medium) entropy-flow rate</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Seifert defines the entropy component of the medium surrounding a system (related to the heat dissipated into that medium) through the work done by the force <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\mathbf{x},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathbf{x},t)</annotation></semantics></math> on the system at some time-dependent temperature <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(t)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{S}^{m}(t)=\frac{1}{T(t)}\int\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)d\mathbf{x}=\frac{1}{D(t)}\int\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)d\mathbf{x}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{S}^{m}(t)=\frac{1}{T(t)}\int\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)d\mathbf{x}=\frac{1}{D(t)}\int\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)d\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In order to make the analogy between the diffusion algorithm and a physical system, we imagine a mobility (inverse friction) constant <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and corresponding Einstein relation <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(t)=\mu T(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(t)=\mu T(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing us to write the drift term <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}=\mu\mathbf{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐅</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}=\mu\mathbf{F}</annotation></semantics></math> in the SDE <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mu\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{x},t)+g(t)d\mathbf{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐅</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mu\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{x},t)+g(t)d\mathbf{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The exchange/flow rate of entropy into the system is just the negative of the one into the medium,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{S}^{e}(t)=-\dot{S}^{m}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>e</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{S}^{e}(t)=-\dot{S}^{m}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{D(t)}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot(\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-D(t)\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{D(t)}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot(\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-D(t)\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{D(t)}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]+\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{D(t)}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]+\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{2}{g(t)^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]+\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{2}{g(t)^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]+\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where in the first line we have use the fact that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)=\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x},t)=\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>System entropy rate</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the expressions for <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{S}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{S}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{S}^{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>e</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{S}^{e}</annotation></semantics></math>, expanding the square and canceling terms gives the simplified equation for the (total) system entropy rate:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{S}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{S}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dot{S}^{i}(t)+\dot{S}^{e}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>e</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dot{S}^{i}(t)+\dot{S}^{e}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D(t)}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-D(t)\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]-\frac{1}{D(t)}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]+\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D(t)}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-D(t)\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]-\frac{1}{D(t)}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]+\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)]+D(t)\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)]+D(t)\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)]+\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)]+\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we have used Stein’s identity for <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)]=-\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)]=-\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\cdot\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x},t)]</annotation></semantics></math> (see Sec. <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Stein’s Identity ‣ Appendix B Lower Bound for Negative Log-Likelihood ‣ Thermodynamic Performance Limits for Score-Based Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Lower Bound for Negative Log-Likelihood</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Log-Likelihood from Probability Flow ODE</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all diffusion processes, there exists a corresponding deterministic process called the probability flow ODE whose trajectories share the same marginal probability densities <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\right\}_{t=0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\right\}_{t=0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> as the SDE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al. [2021]</a></cite>. For the case of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)dt+g(t)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)dt+g(t)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)=\sigma^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)=\sigma^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability flow ODE is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\left[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)-\frac{1}{2}g(t)^{2}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t})\right]dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\left[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)-\frac{1}{2}g(t)^{2}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t})\right]dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The probability flow ODE has the following form when we approximate the score with the score neural network model <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\approx\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\approx\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\underbrace{\left[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)-\frac{1}{2}g(t)^{2}\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]}_{=:\tilde{\mathbf{f}}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)}dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\underbrace{\left[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)-\frac{1}{2}g(t)^{2}\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]}_{=:\tilde{\mathbf{f}}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)}dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">With the instantaneous change of variables formula <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2018</a>]</cite>, we can compute the log-likelihood of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> using</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{0})=\log p_{T}(\mathbf{x}_{T})+\int_{0}^{T}\nabla\cdot\tilde{\mathbf{f}}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\mathrm{d}t" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>∇</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{0})=\log p_{T}(\mathbf{x}_{T})+\int_{0}^{T}\nabla\cdot\tilde{\mathbf{f}}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as a function of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> can be obtained by solving the probability flow ODE. Using <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1</annotation></semantics></math> and the definition of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{f}}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{f}}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> above, the log-likelihood is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log p_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{0})=\log p_{1}(\mathbf{x}_{1})+\int_{0}^{1}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)-\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\nabla\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{0})=\log p_{1}(\mathbf{x}_{1})+\int_{0}^{1}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)-\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\nabla\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>NLL Lower Bound</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The data-average log-likelihood at <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}\left[\log p_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{0}\right)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{p_{1}}\left[\log p_{1}\left(\mathbf{x}_{1}\right)\right]+\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)-\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\nabla\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}\left[\log p_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{0}\right)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{p_{1}}\left[\log p_{1}\left(\mathbf{x}_{1}\right)\right]+\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)-\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\nabla\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The first term is the entropy at <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}=-\mathbb{E}_{p_{1}}\left[\log p_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}=-\mathbb{E}_{p_{1}}\left[\log p_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. We re-express the divergence of the score term using <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}]=-\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}]=-\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> (Stein’s identity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu and Wang, 2016</a>]</cite>), which gives:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{NLL}:=-\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}\left[\log p_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{0}\right)\right]=S_{1}+\int_{0}^{1}\left[-\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]-\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}\right]\right]dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>NLL</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{NLL}:=-\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}\left[\log p_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{0}\right)\right]=S_{1}+\int_{0}^{1}\left[-\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]-\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}\right]\right]dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using one of the polarization identities, <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\cdot\mathbf{s}^{\text{true}}=\frac{1}{2}\left(\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\right\|^{2}+\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}\right\|^{2}-\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}\right\|^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\cdot\mathbf{s}^{\text{true}}=\frac{1}{2}\left(\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\right\|^{2}+\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}\right\|^{2}-\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}\right\|^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{NLL}=S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>NLL</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{NLL}=S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]dt-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[||\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}||^{2}\right]dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]dt-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[||\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}||^{2}\right]dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\mathbf{|}|\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}||^{2}\right]dt+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[||\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}||^{2}\right]dt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\mathbf{|}|\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}||^{2}\right]dt+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[||\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}||^{2}\right]dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\text{true }}\right\|^{2}=\left(S_{1}-S_{0}\right)-\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)]dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true </mtext></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\text{true }}\right\|^{2}=\left(S_{1}-S_{0}\right)-\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)]dt</annotation></semantics></math>, giving</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{NLL}=\frac{S_{0}+S_{1}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>NLL</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{NLL}=\frac{S_{0}+S_{1}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]dt-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[||\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}||^{2}\right]dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]dt-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[||\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}||^{2}\right]dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[||\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}||^{2}\right]dt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[||\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\text{true}}||^{2}\right]dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}=S(p_{0})=S(p_{\text{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}=S(p_{0})=S(p_{\text{data}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(t)=\mathbb{E}[\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)]+\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(t)=\mathbb{E}[\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\cdot\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)]+\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and the non-negativivity of the squared-difference term, we find that the negative log-likelihood obeys the lower bound</p>
<table id="A2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\mathrm{NLL}\geq\frac{S_{0}+S_{1}}{2}-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(t)dt}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>NLL</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\mathrm{NLL}\geq\frac{S_{0}+S_{1}}{2}-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(t)dt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">and the bound is tight when <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=s_{\text{true}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=s_{\text{true}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{NLL}=S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>NLL</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{NLL}=S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For the drift-less diffusion process, <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and the system entropy rate is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(t)=\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{i}(t)=\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|^{2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(t)=\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{i}(t)=\frac{g(t)^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">so the lower bound is given in terms of entropies is</p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\mathrm{NLL}\geq\frac{S_{0}+S_{1}}{2}-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{i}(t)dt.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mi>NLL</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\mathrm{NLL}\geq\frac{S_{0}+S_{1}}{2}-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{i}(t)dt.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Stein’s Identity</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu and Wang, 2016</a>]</cite>, Stein’s identity states that for sufficiently regular <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p}\left[\mathcal{A}_{p}\boldsymbol{\phi}(x)\right]=0,\quad\mathrm{where}\quad\mathcal{A}_{p}\boldsymbol{\phi}(x)=\boldsymbol{\phi}(x)\nabla_{x}\log p(x)^{\top}+\nabla_{x}\boldsymbol{\phi}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>where</mi><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p}\left[\mathcal{A}_{p}\boldsymbol{\phi}(x)\right]=0,\quad\mathrm{where}\quad\mathcal{A}_{p}\boldsymbol{\phi}(x)=\boldsymbol{\phi}(x)\nabla_{x}\log p(x)^{\top}+\nabla_{x}\boldsymbol{\phi}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is called the Stein operator, which acts on function <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and yields a zero mean function <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{p}\phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{p}\phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim p</annotation></semantics></math>. Expanding this identity coordinate-wise, it is exactly the statement:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p}[\nabla\cdot\phi]=-\mathbb{E}_{p}[\phi\cdot s]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p}[\nabla\cdot\phi]=-\mathbb{E}_{p}[\phi\cdot s].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">With the true score <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}=\nabla\log p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}=\nabla\log p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p}[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}]=-\mathbb{E}_{p}\left[\|\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\|^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p}[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}]=-\mathbb{E}_{p}\left[\|\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\|^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For an approximate score <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> :</p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\right]=-\mathbb{E}_{p}\left[\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p}\left[\nabla\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\right]=-\mathbb{E}_{p}\left[\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\cdot\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which equals <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\mathbb{E}_{p}\left[\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\mathbb{E}_{p}\left[\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> only if <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Maxwell’s Demon in Controlled-Forward Process</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al. [2021]</a></cite> use the notation of Haussman-Pardoux / Anderson <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haussmann and Pardoux, 1986</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anderson, 1982</a>]</cite></p>
<table id="A3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}t+g(t)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}_{t}\quad\mathrm{(Forward)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Forward</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}t+g(t)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}_{t}\quad\mathrm{(Forward)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}_{t}=[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}t-g(t)^{2}\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)]\mathrm{d}t+g(t)\mathrm{d}\overline{\mathbf{w}}_{t}\quad\mathrm{(Reverse)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Reverse</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}_{t}=[\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}t-g(t)^{2}\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)]\mathrm{d}t+g(t)\mathrm{d}\overline{\mathbf{w}}_{t}\quad\mathrm{(Reverse)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathbf{w}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathbf{w}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard Wiener process when time is run backwards. <span id="A3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Note</span>, Eq. (8) is usually integrated from <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> down to <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, making <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dt</annotation></semantics></math> negative.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Reverse Process</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have chosen the forward SDE to be</p>
<table id="A3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\sigma^{t}d\mathbf{w}_{t},\quad t\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\sigma^{t}d\mathbf{w}_{t},\quad t\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To sample from our time-dependent score-based model <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we first draw a sample from the prior distribution <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}\approx\mathbf{N}\left(\mathbf{x};\mathbf{0},\frac{1}{2}\left(\sigma^{2}-1\right)\mathbf{I}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}\approx\mathbf{N}\left(\mathbf{x};\mathbf{0},\frac{1}{2}\left(\sigma^{2}-1\right)\mathbf{I}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and then solve the reverse-time SDE with numerical methods. In particular, using our time-dependent score-based model, the reverse-time SDE can be approximated by</p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=-\sigma^{2t}s_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)dt+\sigma^{t}d\overline{\mathbf{w}}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=-\sigma^{2t}s_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)dt+\sigma^{t}d\overline{\mathbf{w}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, one can use numerical methods to solve for the reverse-time SDE, such as the Euler-Maruyama approach. It is based on a simple discretization to the SDE, replacing <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dt</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{0},g^{2}(t)\Delta t\mathbf{I}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{0},g^{2}(t)\Delta t\mathbf{I}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. When applied to our reverse-time SDE, we can obtain the following iteration rule</p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t-\Delta t}=\mathbf{x}_{t}+\sigma^{2t}s_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)\Delta t+\sigma^{t}\sqrt{\Delta t}\mathbf{z}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t-\Delta t}=\mathbf{x}_{t}+\sigma^{2t}s_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)\Delta t+\sigma^{t}\sqrt{\Delta t}\mathbf{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Controlled-Forward Process</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Time always runs forward in the real world: one can achieve a physical realization of the generative process by defining a clock</p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:=T-t,\quad 0\leq\tau\leq T," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:=T-t,\quad 0\leq\tau\leq T,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">such that integrating forward in <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as integrating backward in <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. We plug in <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T-\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T-\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dt=-d\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dt=-d\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\bar{\mathbf{w}}_{t}=d\mathbf{w}_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\bar{\mathbf{w}}_{t}=d\mathbf{w}_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> to re-parameterize reverse Eq. (8) as a controlled-forward process</p>
<table id="A3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau}=[-\mathbf{f}(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau},T-\tau)+g(T-\tau)^{2}\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau},T-\tau)]\mathrm{d}\tau+g(T-\tau)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}_{\tau}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau}=[-\mathbf{f}(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau},T-\tau)+g(T-\tau)^{2}\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau},T-\tau)]\mathrm{d}\tau+g(T-\tau)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau}:=\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau}:=\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Entropy Rates of the Controlled-Forward Process</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the controlled-forward formulation, the drift becomes <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{f}}(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau},\tau)=g(\tau)^{2}\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau},\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{f}}(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau},\tau)=g(\tau)^{2}\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau},\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting this into the general entropy rate expressions derived in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Entropy Rates for Score-Based Diffusion Models ‣ Thermodynamic Performance Limits for Score-Based Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>
yields the simplified relations:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{S}^{i}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\tau)=\frac{g(\tau)^{2}}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau},\tau)\|^{2}\right],\quad\dot{S}^{e}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\tau)=-2\dot{S}^{i}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\tau),\quad\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\tau)=-\dot{S}^{i}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\tau)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{S}^{i}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\tau)=\frac{g(\tau)^{2}}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{\tau},\tau)\|^{2}\right],\quad\dot{S}^{e}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\tau)=-2\dot{S}^{i}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\tau),\quad\dot{S}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\tau)=-\dot{S}^{i}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\tau).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, in the controlled-forward process the system entropy rate is exactly the negative of the intrinsic entropy production rate.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>General Continuous-Time Diffusion Processes</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al. [2021]</a></cite> showed that score-based generative models can be formulated in terms of a general Itô SDE of the form</p>
<table id="A4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{f}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)dt+g(t)d\mathbf{w}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{f}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)dt+g(t)d\mathbf{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is the drift, <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math> the diffusion coefficient, and <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> a standard Wiener process. Two canonical instantiations of this framework correspond to the variance exploding (VE) and variance preserving (VP) processes.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Variance Exploding (VE) SDE</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The VE process is defined by</p>
<table id="A4.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\sqrt{\frac{d}{dt}\sigma^{2}(t)}d\mathbf{w}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=\sqrt{\frac{d}{dt}\sigma^{2}(t)}d\mathbf{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> a non-decreasing variance schedule. Here the drift vanishes, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, while the diffusion coefficient is chosen so that the marginal variance of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> increases monotonically in <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\rightarrow T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\rightarrow T</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance diverges (hence "exploding"), and the distribution approaches a Gaussian prior. This setting is natural when starting from bounded data distributions, since the forward process progressively washes out structure by injecting unbounded noise</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Variance Preserving (VP) SDE</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, the VP process includes both drift and diffusion terms:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t)\mathbf{x}_{t}dt+\sqrt{\beta(t)}d\mathbf{w}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t)\mathbf{x}_{t}dt+\sqrt{\beta(t)}d\mathbf{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive noise-rate schedule. The drift pulls <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> toward the origin at a rate proportional to <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, while the diffusion injects noise of matching strength. This balance ensures that the overall variance of the process remains bounded (and can be normalized to unity) for all <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the forward diffusion maps data smoothly into an isotropic Gaussian prior without variance blow-up.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Both SDEs fit seamlessly into the score-based generative modeling framework. In each case, the reverse-time dynamics introduce an additional score-dependent drift term,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{\tau}=\left[-\mathbf{f}\left(\mathbf{x}_{\tau},T-\tau\right)+g^{2}(T-\tau)\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{\tau}}\log p_{\tau}\left(\mathbf{x}_{\tau}\right)\right]d\tau+g(T-\tau)d\mathbf{w}_{\tau}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{\tau}=\left[-\mathbf{f}\left(\mathbf{x}_{\tau},T-\tau\right)+g^{2}(T-\tau)\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{\tau}}\log p_{\tau}\left(\mathbf{x}_{\tau}\right)\right]d\tau+g(T-\tau)d\mathbf{w}_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the score <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{\tau}}\log p_{\tau}\left(\mathbf{x}_{\tau}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{\tau}}\log p_{\tau}\left(\mathbf{x}_{\tau}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is approximated by a neural network. The VE and VP choices thus represent two distinct, yet complementary, continuous-time noise injection schemes, both of which reduce to the driftless case when <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=0</annotation></semantics></math> and variance is allowed to grow freely. They provide the practical foundation for most modern diffusion models, differing primarily in how variance is managed over time and, correspondingly, in their tradeoffs between sample quality and likelihood.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to the variance exploding (VE) process considered in the main text, we evaluate the variance preserving (VP) process used in denoising diffusion probabilistic models (DDPMs). The VP process is governed by the forward SDE</p>
<table id="A4.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{t}=-\tfrac{1}{2}\beta(t)\,\mathbf{x}_{t}\,dt+\sqrt{\beta(t)}\,d\mathbf{w}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{t}=-\tfrac{1}{2}\beta(t)\,\mathbf{x}_{t}\,dt+\sqrt{\beta(t)}\,d\mathbf{w}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the variance schedule and <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is standard Brownian motion. This process interpolates between the data distribution at <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> and an isotropic Gaussian prior at <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> while preserving variance at each time step. The reverse process is parameterized by the learned score network, and the associated entropy-production integrals are estimated analogously to the VE case.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Constructing the VP Schedule from <math id="A4.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To specify <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we set a desired terminal noise scale <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, which encodes how much Gaussian noise is injected by the end of the forward process.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.1 </span>Integrated noise budget</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The mean-scaling factor of the VP process is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha(t)=\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{t}\beta(u)du\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(t)=\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{t}\beta(u)du\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so at terminal time <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(1)^{2}=\exp(-B),\quad B:=\int_{0}^{1}\beta(u)du" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(1)^{2}=\exp(-B),\quad B:=\int_{0}^{1}\beta(u)du</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The variance contributed by the noise term is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(1)^{2}=1-\alpha(1)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(1)^{2}=1-\alpha(1)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Requiring <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(1)^{2}=\sigma^{2}/1+\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(1)^{2}=\sigma^{2}/1+\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> yields the condition</p>
<table id="A4.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\log\left(1+\sigma^{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\log\left(1+\sigma^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Thus the entire VP schedule is determined by the integrated noise budget <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.2 </span>Linear schedule construction</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A common choice is to make <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> linear in <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)=\beta_{\min}+t\left(\beta_{\max}-\beta_{\min}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)=\beta_{\min}+t\left(\beta_{\max}-\beta_{\min}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The constants <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{min }}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>min </mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{min }}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{max }}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>max </mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{max }}</annotation></semantics></math> are set so that the integral matches the budget:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}\beta(t)dt=\frac{1}{2}\left(\beta_{\min}+\beta_{\max}\right)=B" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}\beta(t)dt=\frac{1}{2}\left(\beta_{\min}+\beta_{\max}\right)=B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Introducing a ratio parameter <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A4.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\min}=rB,\quad\beta_{\max}=(2-r)B," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\min}=rB,\quad\beta_{\max}=(2-r)B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which ensures the correct average while allowing flexibility in the temporal profile of noise injection. Smaller <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> front-loads noise near <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>, while larger <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> distributes noise more evenly across time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the VP formulation, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is the logarithmic noise budget: it quantifies the total exponential damping of the signal. In the VE formulation, the corresponding budget is the variance scale <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The two are linked by <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=e^{B}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>B</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=e^{B}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the VP schedule can be constructed from a single intuitive parameter <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, which specifies the effective strength of the forward noise process, while <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> serves as its natural exponential coordinate.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Standard Gaussian Data</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For validation we include experiments where the data distribution <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard Gaussian. In this case, the score function is exactly linear:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{\text{data}}(\mathbf{x})=-\mathbf{x}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{\text{data}}(\mathbf{x})=-\mathbf{x},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which can be fit by a single-layer neural network with linear weights. This setting provides a ground-truth baseline where the score is known analytically, allowing us to verify the tightness of the lower bound and the accuracy of our numerical estimators.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the case in which the data is normally distributed <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\mu},\boldsymbol{\Sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\mu},\boldsymbol{\Sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> and a drift-less forward process with variance increment <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(t)=\int_{0}^{t}g(u)^{2}du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(t)=\int_{0}^{t}g(u)^{2}du</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{2}(t)=\sigma^{2t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{2}(t)=\sigma^{2t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(t)=\frac{\sigma^{2t}-1}{2\ln\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(t)=\frac{\sigma^{2t}-1}{2\ln\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\mu},\boldsymbol{\Sigma}+v(t)\boldsymbol{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\mu},\boldsymbol{\Sigma}+v(t)\boldsymbol{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A5.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\text{true }}(\mathbf{x},t)=\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=-(\boldsymbol{\Sigma}+v(t)\mathbf{I})^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true </mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\text{true }}(\mathbf{x},t)=\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=-(\boldsymbol{\Sigma}+v(t)\mathbf{I})^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which is exactly linear in <math id="A5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. A tiny network (even a single linear layer conditioned on <math id="A5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>) can represent this perfectly, so training can drive <math id="A5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\rightarrow\mathbf{s}_{\text{true }}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true </mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\rightarrow\mathbf{s}_{\text{true }}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof</span>. Let</p>
<table id="A5.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\mu},\mathbf{C}(t)),\quad\mathbf{C}(t)=\boldsymbol{\Sigma}+v(t)\mathbf{I}_{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\mu},\mathbf{C}(t)),\quad\mathbf{C}(t)=\boldsymbol{\Sigma}+v(t)\mathbf{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric positive-definite. The multivariate Gaussian pdf is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{(2\pi)^{d/2}\operatorname{det}(\mathbf{C})^{1/2}}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})^{\top}\mathbf{C}^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>det</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{(2\pi)^{d/2}\operatorname{det}(\mathbf{C})^{1/2}}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})^{\top}\mathbf{C}^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Take logs:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})^{\top}\mathbf{C}^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})-\frac{1}{2}\log\operatorname{det}(2\pi\mathbf{C})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>det</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})^{\top}\mathbf{C}^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})-\frac{1}{2}\log\operatorname{det}(2\pi\mathbf{C}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Only the quadratic term depends on <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=(x-\mu)_{j}A_{jk}(x-\mu)_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=(x-\mu)_{j}A_{jk}(x-\mu)_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial h}{\partial x_{i}}=A_{ij}(x-\mu)_{j}+A_{ji}(x-\mu)_{j}=\left[\left(A+A^{\top}\right)(x-\mu)\right]_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial h}{\partial x_{i}}=A_{ij}(x-\mu)_{j}+A_{ji}(x-\mu)_{j}=\left[\left(A+A^{\top}\right)(x-\mu)\right]_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.5" class="ltx_p">and we have</p>
<table id="A5.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\left[(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})^{\top}\mathbf{A}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})\right]=\left(\mathbf{A}+\mathbf{A}^{\top}\right)(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})=2\mathbf{A}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})\quad\left(\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{A}^{\top}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\left[(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})^{\top}\mathbf{A}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})\right]=\left(\mathbf{A}+\mathbf{A}^{\top}\right)(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})=2\mathbf{A}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})\quad\left(\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{A}^{\top}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.6" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{C}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{C}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A5.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=-\frac{1}{2}\cdot 2\mathbf{C}^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})=-\mathbf{C}^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=-\frac{1}{2}\cdot 2\mathbf{C}^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})=-\mathbf{C}^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Therefore the true score is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\text{true }}(\mathbf{x},t)=\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=-(\boldsymbol{\Sigma}+v(t)\mathbf{I})^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>true </mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\text{true }}(\mathbf{x},t)=\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})=-(\boldsymbol{\Sigma}+v(t)\mathbf{I})^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.8" class="ltx_p">exactly as claimed.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Exact Score of the Uniform + Normal Distributions</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pixels are independent under Uniform[0,1] and the Gaussian noise factorizes across coordinates, so we consider the 1D case and adopt scalar notation throughout. For the drift-less diffusion,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dx_{t}=g(t)dW_{t},\quad v(t)=\int_{0}^{t}g(u)^{2}du,\quad s=\sqrt{v(t)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dx_{t}=g(t)dW_{t},\quad v(t)=\int_{0}^{t}g(u)^{2}du,\quad s=\sqrt{v(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Conditioned on <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A6.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\mid x_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(x_{0},s^{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\mid x_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(x_{0},s^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If the data is Uniform on <math id="A6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> (density <math id="A6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}(u)=\mathbf{1}_{[0,1]}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}(u)=\mathbf{1}_{[0,1]}(u)</annotation></semantics></math>), the marginal at time <math id="A6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the convolution</p>
<table id="A6.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x)=\int_{0}^{1}\phi_{s}(x-u)du" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x)=\int_{0}^{1}\phi_{s}(x-u)du</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A6.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{s}(z)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}s}\exp\left(-\frac{z^{2}}{2s^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{s}(z)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}s}\exp\left(-\frac{z^{2}}{2s^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p3.3" class="ltx_p">is the <math id="A6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}\left(0,s^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}\left(0,s^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> pdf. With a change of variable <math id="A6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(x-u)/s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(x-u)/s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="du=-sdz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">du=-sdz</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A6.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x)=\int_{(x-1)/s}^{x/s}\phi(z)dz=\Phi\left(\frac{x}{s}\right)-\Phi\left(\frac{x-1}{s}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x)=\int_{(x-1)/s}^{x/s}\phi(z)dz=\Phi\left(\frac{x}{s}\right)-\Phi\left(\frac{x-1}{s}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p3.4" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> the standard normal pdf/cdf.
Differentiate w.r.t. <math id="A6.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> :</p>
<table id="A6.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{x}p_{t}(x)=\frac{1}{s}\left[\phi\left(\frac{x}{s}\right)-\phi\left(\frac{x-1}{s}\right)\right].\lx@nobreakspace" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{x}p_{t}(x)=\frac{1}{s}\left[\phi\left(\frac{x}{s}\right)-\phi\left(\frac{x-1}{s}\right)\right].\lx@nobreakspace</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p3.5" class="ltx_p">The score is the gradient of the log-density,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(x,t)=\partial_{x}\log p_{t}(x)=\frac{\partial_{x}p_{t}(x)}{p_{t}(x)}=\frac{\frac{1}{s}\left[\phi\left(\frac{x}{s}\right)-\phi\left(\frac{x-1}{s}\right)\right]}{\Phi\left(\frac{x}{s}\right)-\Phi\left(\frac{x-1}{s}\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(x,t)=\partial_{x}\log p_{t}(x)=\frac{\partial_{x}p_{t}(x)}{p_{t}(x)}=\frac{\frac{1}{s}\left[\phi\left(\frac{x}{s}\right)-\phi\left(\frac{x-1}{s}\right)\right]}{\Phi\left(\frac{x}{s}\right)-\Phi\left(\frac{x-1}{s}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Numerical Estimates of Exact NLL Terms</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As summarized in Table <a href="#A7.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ G.5.4 Numerical error: floating-point and conditioning ‣ G.5 Error sources ‣ Appendix G Numerical Estimates of Exact NLL Terms ‣ Thermodynamic Performance Limits for Score-Based Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the decomposition includes both exact and estimated terms, with dominant error sources arising from finite-batch sampling, quadrature, and model fit.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Equilibrium entropy <math id="A7.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the forward drift-less diffusion process has covariance <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(1)\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(1)\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="A7.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(1)=\frac{\sigma^{2}-1}{2\ln\sigma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(1)=\frac{\sigma^{2}-1}{2\ln\sigma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence the equilibrium entropy in nats for a <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional Gaussian is</p>
<table id="A7.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1,\mathrm{nats}}=\frac{d}{2}\ln(2\pi ev(1))=\frac{d}{2}\ln\left(2\pi e\frac{\sigma^{2}-1}{2\ln\sigma}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>nats</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1,\mathrm{nats}}=\frac{d}{2}\ln(2\pi ev(1))=\frac{d}{2}\ln\left(2\pi e\frac{\sigma^{2}-1}{2\ln\sigma}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and in bits-per-dimension (bpd),</p>
<table id="A7.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}=\frac{S_{1,\mathrm{nats}}}{d\ln 2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>nats</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}=\frac{S_{1,\mathrm{nats}}}{d\ln 2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">This term is computed analytically. We compute the exact closed form and convert it to bpd.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Dataset entropy <math id="A7.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These constants are independent of the diffusion schedule (VE vs VP) and enter directly into the NLL lower bound formulas. For the standard Gaussian datasets considered, the data entropy is fixed by the closed-form expression</p>
<table id="A7.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}=\frac{1}{2}d\log(2\pi e)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}=\frac{1}{2}d\log(2\pi e)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">corresponding to the entropy of a <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional standard normal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the Uniform <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> datasets, the entropy vanishes, <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, since the density is constant on its support. Let <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mathrm{Unif}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mathrm{Unif}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.
The differential entropy is</p>
<table id="A7.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{0}\;=\;-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p(x)\,\log p(x)\,dx\;=\;-\int_{[0,1]^{d}}1\cdot\log 1\;dx\;=\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}\;=\;-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p(x)\,\log p(x)\,dx\;=\;-\int_{[0,1]^{d}}1\cdot\log 1\;dx\;=\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By factorization across coordinates,
<math id="A7.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}h(X_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}h(X_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}\sim\mathrm{Unif}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}\sim\mathrm{Unif}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A7.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h(X_{i})=-\!\int_{0}^{1}1\cdot\log 1\,dx_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.026em">−</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0.026em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(X_{i})=-\!\int_{0}^{1}1\cdot\log 1\,dx_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Squared-norm of the model score, <math id="A7.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We estimate</p>
<table id="A7.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}g(t)^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}}\left[\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)\right\|^{2}\right]dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}g(t)^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}}\left[\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)\right\|^{2}\right]dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Estimator (per time grid <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<ol id="A7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Draw <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}\sim p_{\mathrm{data}},\mathbf{z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}\sim p_{\mathrm{data}},\mathbf{z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Form <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{0}+\sqrt{v\left(t_{k}\right)}\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{0}+\sqrt{v\left(t_{k}\right)}\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluate the model score <math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t_{k}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t_{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compute the batch mean <math id="A7.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{E}_{k}=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(i)},t_{k}\right)\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{E}_{k}=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(i)},t_{k}\right)\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Finally, we integrate over <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with the trapezoid rule:</p>
<table id="A7.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{k}w_{k}\widehat{E}_{k},\quad w_{k}=g\left(t_{k}\right)^{2}\Delta t_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{k}w_{k}\widehat{E}_{k},\quad w_{k}=g\left(t_{k}\right)^{2}\Delta t_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">and convert to bpd by dividing by <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\ln 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\ln 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>Squared-difference term, <math id="A7.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{diff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>diff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{diff}}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{diff}}=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}g(t)^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}}\left[\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)-\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)\right\|^{2}\right]dt\geq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>diff</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{diff}}=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}g(t)^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}}\left[\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)-\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t},t\right)\right\|^{2}\right]dt\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We estimate it in two ways: directly by computing <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> per sample and average, and using the polarization identity as a sanity check:</p>
<table id="A7.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|a-b\|^{2}=\|a\|^{2}+\|b\|^{2}-2\langle a,b\rangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|a-b\|^{2}=\|a\|^{2}+\|b\|^{2}-2\langle a,b\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">to obtain the the squared difference term from separate estimates of <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\right\|^{2},\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\right\|^{2},\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}},\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}},\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the agreement between the two as a useful consistency diagnostic.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.5 </span>Error sources</h3>

<section id="A7.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.5.1 </span>Finite-batch Monte-Carlo error</h4>

<div id="A7.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a fixed <math id="A7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, the batch mean <math id="A7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{E}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{E}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is an unbiased estimator of <math id="A7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> with variance <math id="A7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\left[\widehat{E}_{k}\right]=\operatorname{Var}[\cdot]/B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\left[\widehat{E}_{k}\right]=\operatorname{Var}[\cdot]/B</annotation></semantics></math>.
Propagating through the trapezoid rule gives an approximate variance</p>
<table id="A7.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\hat{I}]\approx\frac{1}{4}\sum_{k}w_{k}^{2}\frac{\operatorname{Var}_{p_{t_{k}}}\left[U\left(x_{t_{k}},t_{k}\right)\right]}{B},\quad U\in\left\{\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\right\|^{2},\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\|^{2},\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\|^{2}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\hat{I}]\approx\frac{1}{4}\sum_{k}w_{k}^{2}\frac{\operatorname{Var}_{p_{t_{k}}}\left[U\left(x_{t_{k}},t_{k}\right)\right]}{B},\quad U\in\left\{\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\right\|^{2},\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\|^{2},\left\|\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\|^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.5.2 </span>Time-integration (quadrature) error</h4>

<div id="A7.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With a smooth integrand, the trapezoid rule has <math id="A7.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(\Delta t^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(\Delta t^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> bias. Our implementation guards common pitfalls: it clips <math id="A7.SS5.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\left[10^{-4},1-10^{-4}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\left[10^{-4},1-10^{-4}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> to avoid extreme-variance endpoints and integrates with NumPy’s trapezoidal function.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.5.3 </span>Goodness-of-fit (modeling) error</h4>

<div id="A7.SS5.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Only terms that involve <math id="A7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> suffer approximation error:</p>
<ul id="A7.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A7.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> equals the target <math id="A7.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{true}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>true</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{true}}</annotation></semantics></math> iff <math id="A7.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\equiv\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\equiv\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The gap is not simply <math id="A7.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{diff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>diff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{diff}}</annotation></semantics></math> due to the cross-term <math id="A7.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int g(t)^{2}\mathbb{E}\left\langle\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}},\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\rangle dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int g(t)^{2}\mathbb{E}\left\langle\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}-\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}},\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}\right\rangle dt</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice we monitor <math id="A7.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{diff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>diff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{diff}}</annotation></semantics></math> (nonnegative, zero at optimum) and cosine similarity of <math id="A7.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A7.I2.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathrm{true}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>true</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathrm{true}}</annotation></semantics></math> as diagnostics (our code logs min/mean/max cosine).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{diff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>diff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{diff}}</annotation></semantics></math> itself is zero iff the model is perfect; otherwise it is positive and captures a portion of the model-fit error. When <math id="A7.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathrm{true}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>true</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathrm{true}}</annotation></semantics></math> is unavailable (e.g., MNIST), any proxy introduces additional modeling bias on top of Monte-Carlo and quadrature error.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.5.4 </span>Numerical error: floating-point and conditioning</h4>

<div id="A7.SS5.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Computing <math id="A7.SS5.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>true</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\mathrm{true}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the variance-expanded uniform uses <math id="A7.SS5.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi\left(z_{L}\right)-\Phi\left(z_{R}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\left(z_{L}\right)-\Phi\left(z_{R}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>; we clamp the denominator and evaluate in float64 to avoid catastrophic cancellation when <math id="A7.SS5.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is small/large. The network outputs are float32; we upcast to float64 before inner products, which prevents accumulation error in norms and inner products.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A7.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A7.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quantity</span></th>
<th id="A7.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A7.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;">
<span id="A7.T1.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.T1.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Approach</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A7.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A7.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error type(s)</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
